debocker (0.6) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Build with pyproject.toml and package for Debian.
  * Layered package lists with exclusions.
  * Fix Let's Encrypt roots never reaching the CA store; bundle ISRG Root
    X1, X2, YR and YE and disable the expired DST Root CA X3.
  * Use the archive mirrors for end-of-life releases and correct which
    keyring verifies each release; add oracular, plucky, questing,
    resolute and trixie.
  * Run commands with subprocess, exit non-zero on failure, use debootstrap
    instead of qemu-debootstrap, and give images a default CMD.
  * Add the -updates and security suites and upgrade to them (--no-updates
    to skip), build in a .partial directory so failed builds aren't reused,
    and check the qemu binfmt handler before foreign-architecture builds.
  * Allow unauthenticated packages in images whose archive keys have expired,
    and mount /dev/pts for the upgrade.
  * Leave apt's package lists and the host's resolv.conf and hostname out
    of the image.
  * Add tests, run them during the package build, add a release table
    checker, and generate a man page with help2man.

 -- Matthew Shaw <mshaw.cx@gmail.com>  Tue, 20 Oct 2026 23:48:56 -0400
